{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1524215-mythos-mutations","id":1524215,"title":"Mythos Mutations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-17T23:32:56-07:00","id":1524215,"title":"Mythos Mutations","content":"Since Titanic Mutations are a thing, and Mythos characters seem primed and ready for weird body horror, I figured a quick and dirty rule-set for making Mutation rules for Mythos characters was in order. I'm not doing all of the &quot;normal&quot; Callings as well, nor am I doing the Titanic ones again. It's just the Mythos-exclusive Callings like Cosmos that are getting the write-up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Corruptor</span><br /> You are the snake whispering in other's ears, the oozing wounds in the backs of your once allies. The king sits on his throne, paralyzed by the words you speak behind his back.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> Add +1 Enhancement to rolls to convince others to pursue bad plans or paths, including enraging them into attacking.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Without a strong individual to hide behind, you are nothing. Away from a Follower, Guide or positive Fatebinding, you gain +2 Complication to all actions. Failure to buy it off makes your character fall into paralysis, unable to complete the action at the worst time. You gain Momentum if this occurs in a really tense situation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cosmos</span><br /> You devour knowledge. You force knowledge into others. You ARE knowledge, whether forbidden, acceptable, or some shade of both.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> Gain +1 Enhancement to acquire information that is nominally hidden.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> While you CAN transmit information to others, doing so is hazardous. Whenever you teach, inform or otherwise convey important information to other characters, they suffer a Bruised Injury Condition from bleeding ears and eyes. This can only occur once per arc per character.\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Defiler</span><br /> You cultivate disease where others look to cure it. An illness is nothing if it cannot spread to others, and so you encourage the growth of plagues and ideas.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> You gain +1 Enhancement to spread something affecting you, whether an emotion you are currently feeling or an illness you are infected with.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> It's harder for you to recover or help others to do so. Any attempts to perform First Aid BY you or ON you require 2 more successes per Condition.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Torturer</span><br /> You hurt others and enjoy the process of doing so. The more they cry, the better in your eyes.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> Gain +1 Enhancement to attacks.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> You cannot inflict the final Injury to Take Out a character.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Condition:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mythos Gravity</span><br /> The Scion can use their Omen to change the Atmosphere of a situation by 1 in either direction. Doing so makes the Scion's nature obvious, and treats their Legend/Awareness as 2 higher for the purpose of strengthening Fatebindings for the affected characters, Mythos or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}